{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'POSE_PROJECT_ROOT|--root|project-root' pose-mcp/internal/cli/cli.go pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/root.go; git diff --numstat; nl -ba .pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md | tail -15; rg -n 'POSE_PROJECT_ROOT' pose-mcp/internal/cli | head -15\"","aggregated_output":"rg: pose-mcp/internal/cli/root.go: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n3\t2\t.pose/assessments/README.md\n12\t10\t.pose/assessments/consolidated.md\n66\t432\t.pose/assessments/integrations.md\n2\t2\t.pose/assessments/pose-mcp.md\n6\t6\t.pose/assessments/technical-debt.md\n7\t7\t.pose/state/components/pose-mcp.json\n127\t615\t.pose/state/integrations.json\n6\t6\t.pose/state/technical-debt.json\n   247\t### Delivered scope\n   248\t`pose validate --carry` refreshes the canonical structured result. It runs the modules the changed-scope rules select since the canonical base and carries the other checks with their outcome and the head where they ran. The changed set ignores the result file and the derived administrative records that material bindings already ignore. Any doubt about the base runs everything, and the record says why. Modules can declare `selfContained` to stop being widened by changes outside every module. The delivery index reads a carried result as an observation of its own head. The record now names the engine version together with its build revision.\n   249\t\n   250\t### Files and modules changed\n   251\t`pose-mcp/internal/cli` (validate, its scope selection, its result fields and the help catalogue), `pose-mcp/internal/pose` (the delivery reading of the result), the manual in English and pt-BR with their embedded copies, this spec and its ADR.\n   252\t\n   253\t### Validation executed\n   254\tSee the execution log: the package tests with mutation checks, the full `go test ./...` and the strict matrix with 236 of 236 checks.\n   255\t\n   256\t### Residual risks\n   257\tAn instance that declares a module self-contained while its checks read files outside it would carry a stale result. The declaration is explicit and documented, and the default stays the full fallback.\n   258\t\n   259\t### Follow-ups\n   260\t- [open] F1: cover with an end-to-end test that a review bundle sealed over a carried record judges the carried head (seal, verify and closeout-check on a fixture). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-15)\n   261\t- [open] F2: `--carry --report` lists carried checks as executed commands without their `carried_from` head and time; exclude them from the executed summary and label reused results (review round 13, N39). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-15)\npose-mcp/internal/cli/project_id_directory_name_test.go:33:\tfor _, key := range []string{\"POSE_PROJECT_ROOT\", \"POSE_PROJECT_ROOTS\", \"POSE_DEFAULT_PROJECT_ID\", \"HARNE8_PROJECTS_DIR\"} {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/assess.go:466:// portfolio projection (self + scanned projects dir + POSE_PROJECT_ROOTS).\npose-mcp/internal/cli/assess.go:477:\t\t\t\"Error: project %q is not an authorized root (self, HARNE8_PROJECTS_DIR scan, or POSE_PROJECT_ROOTS)\\n\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/assess.go:478:\t\t\t\"Erro: projeto %q não é um root autorizado (self, scan de HARNE8_PROJECTS_DIR, ou POSE_PROJECT_ROOTS)\\n\"), projectID)\npose-mcp/internal/cli/artifact_attributions_test.go:21:\tt.Setenv(\"POSE_PROJECT_ROOTS\", \"\")\npose-mcp/internal/cli/cli_test.go:226:\tif env[\"KEEP\"] != \"yes\" || env[\"POSE_PROJECT_ROOT\"] != root || env[\"POSE_DEFAULT_PROJECT_ID\"] != \"proj.test\" {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/multirepo_agent_flow_test.go:68:\tt.Setenv(\"POSE_PROJECT_ROOTS\", roots)\npose-mcp/internal/cli/multirepo_agent_flow_test.go:123:\tt.Setenv(\"POSE_PROJECT_ROOTS\", agentRootsJSON(t, map[string]string{\"proj.executor\": executor, \"proj.sibling\": sibling}))\npose-mcp/internal/cli/multirepo_agent_flow_test.go:150:\tt.